<article class="env-lemma" id="073H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/073H">Lemma <span data-tag="073H">69.8.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be an affine morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Then $R^ if_*\mathcal{F} = 0$ for $i > 0$ and any quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Recall that an affine morphism of algebraic spaces is representable. Hence this follows from (<a href="/tag/071Z" data-tag="071Z">69.3.0.1</a>) and Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01XC" data-tag="01XC">30.2.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>